Z||000000||btoth||04-06-2001||02:29 PM||||Well, I knew it.  My V6 started knocking a few days ago.  And of course this is right after fixing my dew strips and my leaking trunk and bought a new muffler and I was hoping that this week, since it's so warm out, that I <I>might</I> be able to finally install the new quarter windows that I got for Christmas.  <P>Well, I had to drive the car to school today because there was no other car around.  I didn't want to, but I couldn't miss my econ class.  Well, it was just hapily knocking on the way there (mostly just sounding like a beater) but on the way home, at a red light, all hell broke loose.<P>Now it sounds just like a bunch of marbles in my engine.  I'm surprised though... still feels like I have plenty of power and it runs ok.<P>Oh well, just had to let someone know... I don't think this week can get any worse.  Two weeks ago I had my wisdom teeth out, that sucked (mostly just because I couldn't eat any <I>real</I> food).  Then last week it took me forever to find a custom exhaust place that would install my flowmaster, which I never did get installed because my stupid engine started knocking.  Endless frustration.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Thanks for the space. <p>[This message has been edited by btoth (edited 04-06-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000001||Kelvin Vivian||04-06-2001||07:49 PM||||Just a simple check would be to make sure that the car is full of oil...<P>After an oil change, the fellas didn't fill her up all the way and I got this knocking sound in my V6, once it was filled up, she ran smoothly, knocking sound gone.||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||04-06-2001||09:39 PM||||That description sounds like timing chain. Tends to get quieter when it warm, louder cold.||||reg||1
